# Copy to .env (alongside this file) to override. Unset variables fall back to the defaults below.

# The port Apache listens on inside the container, and the host port it's published on.
#UPHPTIME_HTTP_PORT=48484

# Set these to your host user's id/group if you want to edit files under ./data/primary directly
# without sudo (docker-entrypoint.sh re-points www-data at them on startup). Named PUID/PGID, not
# UID/GID: UID is a read-only shell variable in bash, so `UID=1000 docker compose up` silently fails
# to set it.
#PUID=1000
#PGID=1000

# HTTPS, directly - no reverse proxy (see "HTTPS, directly" in the main README for full detail). Drop
# your own cert/key (e.g. a Cloudflare Origin CA cert + its separate intermediate) at
# ./data/primary/config/ssl/{cert.pem,privkey.pem,chain.pem} (chain.pem optional) and uncomment the
# 443 port line in ../docker-compose.yml - that's it, no env vars needed for the default filenames.
# If your files are named differently (e.g. a .key extension) or live elsewhere, point these at them
# directly instead of renaming anything:
#UPHPTIME_HTTPS_PORT=443
#UPHPTIME_TLS_CERT_FILE=/var/www/html/config/ssl/mycert.pem
#UPHPTIME_TLS_KEY_FILE=/var/www/html/config/ssl/mykey.key
#UPHPTIME_TLS_CHAIN_FILE=/var/www/html/config/ssl/intermediate.pem
